 made me feel safe  and that in that moment really i just i  fell head over heels in love with brett  a love that led kitty to bake loaf  after loaf  after loaf a skill which quickly  inspired her to launch her very first  pop-up and about half an hour before the  pop-up the whole town was just empty it  was so nerve-wrecking and slightly  heartbreaking and then i opened the door  and there's about 60 people stretching  all the way down the high street and we  sold out of everything within i think it  was 28 minutes wow 28 minutes and  what was going through your mind  not a lot but at the end i suddenly  realized that this i could i could do  this  yeah this wasn't something that was  helping me get through depression  anxiety this is what i wanted to do  so kitty and al turned to kickstarter  with this one-of-a-kind very  orange-themed fundraising video  within 48 hours we had hit our target  but they also needed a business plan and  who better to ask for advice than the  founders of san francisco's beloved  tartine bakery so i managed to track  down chad robertson and his wife liz  perez so i started write letters just  saying that i love that book how much it  helped me and then one day i looked at  my instagram and i saw that they were  following me  and then chad sent me a message and liz  pruitt when i did the crowd funding put  it onto her instagram story and i'm  still so thankful to them gratitude  which inspired kitty and al to author  their own book of recipes called bread  song  a title inspired by the snap crackle and  pop of bread fresh out of the oven  one of their most popular breads is made  using one of kitty's favorite  ingredients miso the japanese fermented  soybean paste  and then one day i'll say okay i love it  so much why not just like fold it into  the dough  really beautiful like you can actually  see it in in the crumb you get this  amazing red miso swirls look you get  like a little patch here and it makes it  bread incredibly moist too right i mean  miso and a loaf of bread they just not  something i would ever even think about  you can just see that right through  there  that beautiful miso just layered through  [Music]  kitty's sense of humor is baked into  several of her creations  including these  here we've got corgi butter butts corgi  butter butt  as in but  but  i'm a corgi  because you have recorded because i have  a cookie so i have a queen's  exactly so it's this really soft fluffy  brioche and then with a bit of pearl  sugar which is like rock salt for like  rock sugar and choc chips for pores  oh it  is you go hey  how cute is that so cute  this is so good  i mean it's just good  [Laughter]  it's chewy it's sweet  the sugar just really gives it a nice  crunch to it i mean just  it also kind of tastes a bit like  childhood right for kitty the crippling  depression she endured as a 14 year old  will never be entirely gone and  awareness she finds strength  this whole journey started because of  mental health what do you want to say to  those who might be struggling it can get  better and i don't know exactly when but  i know that it will and actually all the  stuff that is you're going through it  does make you stronger because it means  that you can understand others it's just  something that is extra like an extra  flavor to the bread  for sebia saturday morning emphio's tab  waddlington oxfordshire  we love her we love her we love her how  joyful i mean to see that and that it  was depression that brought her to bread  in the first place her father  leaving his job for her  success success success whatever it  takes that's beautiful family i mean  she's just you just want to just eat her  up you know she's so adorable i want to  eat the bread i was just going to say i  want to eat up the bread you could eat  her or the bread and the bread yeah  fantastic she really is nice job

